  "acceptance_met": [
    "Confluent Protobuf indexes follow the generic five-byte header: canonical special [0], signed zigzag count/indexes, top-level and nested declaration-order paths. Independent pinned Confluent MessageIndexes checks exact encode/decode bytes and payload boundary.",
    "Default 1 MiB frame / 32-index path; validated hard maxima 64 MiB / 1024 indexes. Decode borrows payload and reserves only a bounded path after count/remaining-byte checks. Encode and selected-codec exact length are checked before output reservation. Negative, truncated, overflowing, over-limit and invalid-path errors are structured.",
    "Adapter binds an explicitly chosen Codec and known writer schema ID/message path. Unknown IDs and other paths fail before payload decoding; codecs receive an exact bounded payload slice for encoding. No serializer dependency, root/companion manifest or lockfile change, implicit registration, descriptor parser or recursive reference fetch.",
    "Independent Google protoc payloads for top-level strings, empty defaults, and nested Envelope using imported common.Metadata decode via Rust fixture-only codecs; actual Rust-emitted payloads decode with Google and frames decode with Confluent in the reverse direction. Framing-only wide-index boundaries are explicitly separate from descriptor-valid cells."
  ],
